cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use palimpsest in scholarly work, please cite the software using the
  metadata in this file.
title: "palimpsest: Typography-first collation for literary texts"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rivero
    given-names: Joaquín
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-11
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jQuinRivero/palimpsest"
url: "https://jquinrivero.github.io/palimpsest/"
abstract: >-
  An open-source application for comparing two witnesses of a literary text
  with word-level revision, moved/split/merged passage detection, synoptic and
  unified reading, and TEI P5 export.
keywords:
  - collation
  - digital humanities
  - literary criticism
  - textual criticism
  - TEI
